CIA Study – Mandatory Update Setup (v1.3.3 / versionCode 7)

WHAT THIS SOURCE CHANGE DOES
- Checks an HTTPS update metadata URL when the app starts and when it returns to the foreground.
- If internet is unavailable or the metadata endpoint cannot be reached, the app can be used offline.
- If update.json reports a versionCode greater than the installed version, the app is blocked by a non-cancelable “Update Required” dialog. The user must tap “Update Now”.
- The update link opens in the browser. Android may require the user to approve installing updates from that source and confirm installation.
- App data is not intentionally cleared by this update flow. Updating must use the same applicationId and signing key as the installed APK.

REQUIRED BEFORE RELEASE
1. Create a GitHub repository.
2. Upload the new APK as a GitHub Release asset (HTTPS link).
3. Replace YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME and YOUR_REPOSITORY in:
   app/src/main/java/com/ciastudytrainer/app/UpdateChecker.java
   with the actual account and repository.
4. Add update.json to the repository's main branch, with this exact structure:
   {
     "versionCode": 7,
     "versionName": "1.3.3",
     "apkUrl": "https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/releases/download/v1.3.3/CIA-Study-v1.3.3.apk"
   }
5. For every future release, increase versionCode, update versionName, upload the APK, and update update.json.
6. Ensure every update is signed with the same private signing key used for the currently installed app.

IMPORTANT LIMITATION
The update endpoint is a placeholder until configured. The source ZIP is not a signed APK and cannot be installed directly. The APK link is opened externally; Android's installer confirmation cannot be bypassed by a normal app. Test updates on a device with the existing app installed before sharing broadly.
